{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions","id":1010016,"title":"Some custom devotions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-29T17:46:14-08:00","id":1010016,"title":"Some custom devotions","content":"Heya! I dreamed up two custom Devotions that I'd like to throw out for you to critique. Both are aimed at the upper ancilla/lower elder kind of power level.<br /> <br /> <b>Immortal Shape of the Wraith</b><br /> (Protean \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Celerity \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> For a moment, the vampire is no more substantial than mist, causing attacks to pass through her harmlessly.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3 Vitae<br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <b>Action: </b>Reflexive<br /> This Devotion allows a Vampire to become completely immune to one attack, as instead of hitting a solid body, it strikes through a body as substantial as mist. No matter what type of damage is delivered, it deals none, unless the source is from a Bane, in which case it deals normal damage.<br /> This Devotion also allows a Vampire to slip out of a Grapple, as there is no longer any body to hold onto.<br /> This Devotion costs 4 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> Basically, a cheaper, one-attack-only Juggernaut's Gait, with the small benefit that she can't be knocked down, grappled, or driven over an edge by being rammed with a car.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Body of Whispers</b><br /> (Auspex \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Protean \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Normally, a vampire projecting her mind elsewhere, leaves her body dangerously vulnerable. With this Devotion, that is somewhat alleviated by bringing it with her where she goes.<br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Vitae<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Intelligence + Occult + Auspex<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Vampire becomes trapped in a half-ephemeral state, parts of her body shifting in and out of Twilight. She suffers the Stunned Tilt for a number of turns equal to 15 minus her Stamina. During this time both material and Twilight creatures may freely interact with her.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Her body stays rigidly solid.<br /> <b>Success: </b>For a scene, the vampire's body shifts into Twilight, becoming immaterial. During this time the vampire can walk through physical obstacles, and even sink into the ground if she wishes, otherwise she moves just as normal. While in this state, she can not interact with the physical world in any way, though her Disciplines work just the same as normal.<br /> When this Devotion ends, the kindred simply slips back into the world where she happens to be at the moment. If she is inside an object, she will safely appear outside it.<br /> She may end this Devotion at any time she wishes.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Her body submits further to the rule of the mind, her Speed is multiplied by her Auspex dots, and she is no longer limited to obeying gravity.<br /> This Devotion costs 4 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> I wanted an infiltration power. Applying the Twilight Projection to Beast's Skin felt like the most logical step. It is more limited however, one can't stay in this shape forever, and one is much slower. Even with the Exceptional effect the Vampire lacks a lot of the mobility of this shape.<br /> The secondary benefit of this power is that one can chase away pesky spies using the normal Twilight Projection, provided one can catch them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T23:32:39-08:00","id":1010072,"title":"","content":"I like them. <br /> One of my PC has exactly the first one (but celerity 2 as prerequisite) and it could be used also to go through a cage, gate or a wire mesh during a run as a reflexive action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T02:20:21-08:00","id":1010118,"title":"","content":"I like the idea behind the Wraith devotions. The only problem I see is that, apart from escaping when already Grappled, Celerity already does the job of fending of an attack. I'm not completely sure how this is a different ability, other than a more fluffed out and expensive ability. Especially if the prereq. is Celerity 3. Maybe I misunderstand?<br /> <br /> Or wait, is it because the attack can be negated, <i>after </i>damage is done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:25:23-08:00","id":1010129,"title":"","content":"I think it's a perfect effect, like juggernaut gait. The attack is made and hit, and, reflexively, the blow pass your body without damages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:27:34-08:00","id":1010130,"title":"","content":"Body of Whispers feels a little bit out of place, mainly because it almost completely replaces Auspex 5 original power. Instead, why not have the body transform into an animal (one of the forms you posses) and the animal is protective of itself and whatever Den you chose it for? That way, it adds defensive capability, without completely replacing the power (as you'll sometimes decide it's not worthwhile to pay extra just for body to move) but it still has the weakness of &quot;there's something else to kill.&quot; <br /> <br /> As is, you'll always add that one Vitae (unless you want to add WP into the cost) just for that sure protection","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T03:34:27-08:00","id":1010135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010118#post1010118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea behind the Wraith devotions. The only problem I see is that, apart from escaping when already Grappled, Celerity already does the job of fending of an attack. I'm not completely sure how this is a different ability, other than a more fluffed out and expensive ability. Especially if the prereq. is Celerity 3. Maybe I misunderstand?<br /> <br /> Or wait, is it because the attack can be negated, <i>after </i>damage is done?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I was thinking that it's a damage negator, just like Juggernaut's Gait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010130#post1010130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Body of Whispers feels a little bit out of place, mainly because it almost completely replaces Auspex 5 original power. Instead, why not have the body transform into an animal (one of the forms you posses) and the animal is protective of itself and whatever Den you chose it for? That way, it adds defensive capability, without completely replacing the power (as you'll sometimes decide it's not worthwhile to pay extra just for body to move) but it still has the weakness of &quot;there's something else to kill.&quot;<br /> <br /> As is, you'll always add that one Vitae (unless you want to add WP into the cost) just for that sure protection</div> </div> </div> </div>It is also much slower, lasts for a much shorter time, and it takes an exceptional to allow flight. It also removes the &quot;Ah well, I have nothing to lose by spying&quot; angle of Auspex 5. It also doesn't let the Vampire be up during the day, like the original Auspex 5 implies.<br /> <br /> So I think it's different enough that one would want both.<br /> <br /> <br /> But protecting the body isn't what I had it in mind for, I wanted an infiltration power, to make sure that people could never feel truly safe.<br /> I like the paranoid part of vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T05:35:30-08:00","id":1010160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010135#post1010135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I was thinking that it's a damage negator, just like Juggernaut's Gait.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It is also much slower, lasts for a much shorter time, and it takes an exceptional to allow flight. It also removes the &quot;Ah well, I have nothing to lose by spying&quot; angle of Auspex 5. It also doesn't let the Vampire be up during the day, like the original Auspex 5 implies.<br /> <br /> So I think it's different enough that one would want both.<br /> <br /> <br /> But protecting the body isn't what I had it in mind for, I wanted an infiltration power, to make sure that people could never feel truly safe.<br /> I like the paranoid part of vampire society.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ok, that's valid.. but if you're buying such an expensive power, why not get Protean 5 instead? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> No need to buy Auspex at all, and if you do, then you can just use both separately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T07:58:23-08:00","id":1010204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010118#post1010118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea behind the Wraith devotions. The only problem I see is that, apart from escaping when already Grappled, Celerity already does the job of fending of an attack. I'm not completely sure how this is a different ability, other than a more fluffed out and expensive ability. Especially if the prereq. is Celerity 3. Maybe I misunderstand?<br /> <br /> Or wait, is it because the attack can be negated, <i>after </i>damage is done?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking this as well. Why get hit at all when celerity 1 does the same effect. Instead of having it pass through you, why not just... not be there for them to hit you at all. Even if it's a bane source. They have a flame thrower, celerity, boom, you're not there. Instead of taking normal damage.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010135#post1010135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. I was thinking that it's a damage negator, just like Juggernaut's Gait.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> now if it negated <b>all </b>attacks until your next turn.. that would be most powerful.<br /> <br /> Does this power have 1/scene? 1/turn?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions#post1010016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Body of Whispers</b><br /> (Auspex \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, Protean \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Normally, a vampire projecting her mind elsewhere, leaves her body dangerously vulnerable. With this Devotion, that is somewhat alleviated by bringing it with her where she goes.<br /> <b>Cost: </b>3 Vitae<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Intelligence + Occult + Auspex<br /> <b>Action: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Vampire becomes trapped in a half-ephemeral state, parts of her body shifting in and out of Twilight. She suffers the Stunned Tilt for a number of turns equal to 15 minus her Stamina. During this time both material and Twilight creatures may freely interact with her.<br /> <b>Failure:</b> Her body stays rigidly solid.<br /> <b>Success: </b><b>For a scene, the vampire's body shifts into Twilight, becoming immaterial. During this time the vampire can walk through physical obstacles, and even sink into the ground if she wishes, otherwise she moves just as normal.</b> While in this state, she can not interact with the physical world in any way, though her Disciplines work just the same as normal.<br /> When this Devotion ends, the kindred simply slips back into the world where she happens to be at the moment. If she is inside an object, she will safely appear outside it.<br /> She may end this Devotion at any time she wishes.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>Her body submits further to the rule of the mind, <b>her Speed is multiplied by her Auspex dots, and she is no longer limited to obeying gravity.</b><br /> This Devotion costs 4 Experiences to learn.<br /> <br /> I wanted an infiltration power. Applying the Twilight Projection to Beast's Skin felt like the most logical step. It is more limited however, one can't stay in this shape forever, and one is much slower. Even with the Exceptional effect the Vampire lacks a lot of the mobility of this shape.<br /> The secondary benefit of this power is that one can chase away pesky spies using the normal Twilight Projection, provided one can catch them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am on the boat of why not take Protean 5 and be mist or smoke or something, then you can fly and move through cracks? Or Auspex 5 allows you to fly and move through things too...<br /> <br /> I am not sure what you would gain from taking this devotion other than taking your body with you. So much of it is already worded as Auspex 5. If you wanted the Infiltration that is Auspex 5 all the way. You can do everything you had written without needing an exceptional.<br /> <br /> I do have one question, you have &quot;Can not interact with the physical world in any way, but disciplines work the same.&quot; Does that mean you can Awe or Dread presence? Celerity to go faster?<br /> <br /> If you want to take a Devotion to take your body with you, just make that an Auspex 5 devotion + Vigor 1 or 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-30-2016, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:29:33-08:00","id":1010211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010204#post1010204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking this as well. Why get hit at all when celerity 1 does the same effect. Instead of having it pass through you, why not just... not be there for them to hit you at all. Even if it's a bane source. They have a flame thrower, celerity, boom, you're not there. Instead of taking normal damage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> now if it negated <b>all </b>attacks until your next turn.. that would be most powerful.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, using celerity you can move out of the attack range and evade it but you can't attack back because move away is an instant action that you can do before your enemies turn. With this devotion you, reflexively, evade the attack stayng still in the same place and you can attack back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:37:48-08:00","id":1010213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010211#post1010211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, using celerity you can move out of the attack range and evade it but you can't attack back because move away is an instant action that you can do before your enemies turn. With this devotion you, reflexively, evade the attack stayng still in the same place and you can attack back.</div> </div> </div> </div>See the other Celerity thread. You most definitely can Move and attack. You are allowed a Reflexive and Instant action in a turn. So you may move behind someone (reflexive), Evading their attack completely, and hit them upside the head (instant)..<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Celerity<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of<br /> her own. <b>This could be an attack</b>, making it possible to disable an<br /> opponent in mid-action. <b>It may be movement,</b> avoiding harm by<br /> shifting out of reach. Or it could be <b>any other instant action</b>, like<br /> activating a Discipline or dodging. <b>However, the vampire is still<br /> limited to one instant action</b>. She <b>cannot </b>use Celerity to make <b>two<br /> attacks</b>, or an attack followed by another instant action. Likewise she<br /> cannot move further in a single turn than her Speed would allow. &quot;</i><br /> <br /> reiterating: Since moving is not an instant action, you are allowed to move and attack.<br /> You would also be allowed to try to hand-wrack or stun your opponent making them further lose their actions and not just miss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 11-30-2016, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T17:49:43-08:00","id":1010427,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Shattered Fog from VtM. That switched you to mist for the remainder of the round as a reflexive action. There is some utility to that if you can also boost your initiative when solidifying to attack... Maybe even gain surprise on one target?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-01T08:14:39-08:00","id":1010651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1010016-some-custom-devotions?p=1010427#post1010427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Shattered Fog from VtM. That switched you to mist for the remainder of the round as a reflexive action. There is some utility to that if you can also boost your initiative when solidifying to attack... Maybe even gain surprise on one target?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Celerity 1, you can go first. If they dont know you are attacking, it's a surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}